{
  "sourceId": "post-troubleshooting-terraform-en",
  "locale": "en",
  "source": {
    "kind": "single-post",
    "postId": "troubleshooting-terraform"
  },
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Terraform is a great tool for managing infrastructure as code, but sometimes it can be tricky to debug when things go wrong.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In this blog post, I'll share tips on how to troubleshoot Terraform issues.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The TF_LOG environment variable allows you to set the log level for Terraform, which can be useful for getting more details about what Terraform is doing behind the scenes.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "You can set it to one of these values: TRACE , DEBUG , INFO , WARN , or ERROR .",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The default is INFO , which only shows high-level messages.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "To get more verbose output, you can set it to DEBUG .",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "TRACE has details from DEBUG but includes dependency analysis details that are not needed for most debugging.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "For example, you can run this command before running Terraform:",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "export TF_LOG=DEBUG and then terraform plan",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "or run it in a single line",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "export TF_LOG=DEBUG && terraform plan",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "If you specify the TF_LOG_PATH environment variable, logs will be stored in the file.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The debug log can be massive and over 100MB!",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "If you would like to focus on debugging a provider, you should use TF_LOG_PROVIDER with arguments from TF_LOG .",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "If you suspect a problem with dependencies, you should use TF_LOG_CORE .",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Terraform analyzes dependencies between Terraform modules before execution.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Dependency analysis ensures resources are provisioned in the correct order.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, Terraform uses the analysis results for efficient parallel execution of operations by identifying independent sets of resources that can be provisioned or modified concurrently.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "However, logs from concurrent execution are very difficult to read, and we have to disable the concurrency with the parameter -parallelism=1 on plan and apply .",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "With -parallelism=1 , resources are created/modified/destroyed one at a time, in sequence.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "This allows for easier debugging and troubleshooting, as each resource is executed one at a time.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "e.g., terraform apply -parallelism=1 :↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "When -parallelism is not specified, the default value is 10.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The resources are created/modified/destroyed in parallel, allowing for faster execution.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "However, this can also make it more difficult to debug and troubleshoot issues, as multiple resources are executed simultaneously.",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "e.g., terraform apply :↵ ↵",
      "sourceRef": {
        "type": "post",
        "id": "troubleshooting-terraform",
        "title": "Troubleshooting Terraform",
        "url": "/blog/troubleshooting-terraform/"
      }
    }
  ],
  "hasMore": false,
  "totalCount": 27
}